WEBVTT

00:12.510 --> 00:16.500
Huey, once we reach the hospital, 
you can get some rest.

00:16.500 --> 00:17.920
Thank you, ma'am.

00:21.190 --> 00:23.290
A traveling carnival, eh?

00:25.510 --> 00:28.420
You wanted to see that, didn't you? How lucky.

00:29.380 --> 00:31.800
What's lucky about these legs?

00:44.000 --> 00:45.730
I'm very sorry.

00:45.730 --> 00:47.380
Huh? For what?

00:47.380 --> 00:49.720
We will need to inspect your carry-on luggage.

00:50.250 --> 00:52.590
Should we not have brought the chocolate?

00:53.100 --> 00:54.070
This way.

00:55.620 --> 00:56.660
Right in here.

00:56.660 --> 00:58.410
Why, thank you.

00:58.410 --> 00:59.680
Hey, you're...

00:59.680 --> 01:01.240
Ah, I get it.

01:01.240 --> 01:03.250
I see you did your job. Good for you.

01:03.600 --> 01:05.170
Got Viola's id?

01:13.390 --> 01:14.590
Duly received.

01:15.030 --> 01:16.720
I do apologize for the imposition.

01:16.720 --> 01:19.030
Have a lovely trip, now.

01:19.030 --> 01:20.720
Thanks a lot.

01:26.270 --> 01:28.100
Hey, it's the little bird!

01:28.780 --> 01:30.720
My outside persona, Mk II.

01:32.990 --> 01:34.030
Hello?

01:34.720 --> 01:36.570
No, not a problem.

01:37.560 --> 01:39.320
Yes, it's finished.

01:39.900 --> 01:40.990
Yes.

01:41.750 --> 01:43.730
Yes, it has been received.

01:44.380 --> 01:46.750
No, thank you very much.

01:47.060 --> 01:49.760
Yes. Thank you.

01:50.280 --> 01:52.140
Goodbye, then.

01:53.530 --> 01:54.590
Was that Gene?

01:54.590 --> 01:58.170
He's not "Gene." 
He's Vice-Director Junghardt.

01:58.170 --> 02:00.010
Keep business and private matters separate.

02:00.630 --> 02:01.890
So...

02:02.740 --> 02:03.690
What did he say?

02:03.690 --> 02:04.820
About what?

02:04.820 --> 02:08.900
Well, I mean... Work's been 
going really well, so...

02:08.900 --> 02:13.020
I was just wondering what 
he thought about that...

02:13.020 --> 02:14.640
I guess.

02:16.910 --> 02:19.240
Your big brother said he has high hopes.

02:20.190 --> 02:21.390
Really?!

02:21.390 --> 02:23.020
Yeah. For me.

02:23.020 --> 02:26.000
He said to keep taking good care of you.

02:26.260 --> 02:27.560
What?!

04:07.580 --> 04:08.900
Nius...

04:09.550 --> 04:12.490
Achillus... Viola...

04:12.920 --> 04:16.580
The Immortal Nine... The nine who never die.

04:18.000 --> 04:19.150
No...

04:20.160 --> 04:21.960
I guess it's really six now.

04:23.220 --> 04:24.590
<i>Vice-Director Junghardt.</i>

04:25.070 --> 04:29.510
<i>We've received a report that the id 
retrieved from Viola has left Mars.</i>

04:29.510 --> 04:32.840
<i>But Ochrona seems to be 
nosing around, as well.</i>

04:34.480 --> 04:37.150
We certainly wouldn't want 
them finding out about it.

04:37.150 --> 04:38.770
<i>Measures will be taken.</i>

04:39.240 --> 04:41.880
<i>Also, regarding the traveling carnival...</i>

04:41.880 --> 04:43.730
<i>The town where Rouge currently is...</i>

04:44.130 --> 04:46.510
They're putting on a show 
in Wellstown, right?

04:47.060 --> 04:50.640
And that doesn't seem to be mere coincidence.

04:52.200 --> 04:57.440
It seems we'll find a lead on our next target,
Phantom Verde, in the Nean settlement.

04:57.440 --> 05:01.120
Don't the Immortal Nine take human forms?

05:01.460 --> 05:05.390
They might be hiding among the Neans, 
disguised as Neans.

05:07.450 --> 05:09.760
That's Investigator Ash from Ochrona.

05:09.760 --> 05:12.520
He sure went to a lot of trouble, 
coming all the way to Mars.

05:13.190 --> 05:15.020
He's from Ochrona?

05:16.370 --> 05:18.850
Hm? Oh, I saw him on the list.

05:18.850 --> 05:22.560
Something about an old man 
on the rebound, or something.

05:23.510 --> 05:26.270
Neans, Neans, Neans.

05:26.270 --> 05:28.280
What the hell is going on?

05:28.280 --> 05:29.520
Of course they're here.

05:29.520 --> 05:33.030
The biggest Nean settlement 
on Mars is in this city.

05:34.000 --> 05:37.310
Bet you're thrilled to have so many 
of your own kind around, huh?

05:39.050 --> 05:44.040
You have to go through a heavily 
guarded gate to enter the settlement.

05:44.410 --> 05:48.210
Only registered Neans and authorized 
personnel can pass through.

05:51.170 --> 05:52.970
What did Gene say?

05:52.970 --> 05:54.540
Dumped it all on us.

05:54.540 --> 05:58.890
Seriously. Don't come up with 
only half a date plan, damn it.

06:05.640 --> 06:08.360
Whole boiled herm is so good!

06:09.160 --> 06:12.190
Huh? It's gone... It's gone!

06:14.260 --> 06:15.240
Huh?

06:15.240 --> 06:17.120
My chocolate is gone.

06:17.570 --> 06:19.140
I know I still had more!

06:19.140 --> 06:21.580
Your chocolate? Oh, I know where that is.

06:22.660 --> 06:23.970
Here you go.

06:23.970 --> 06:25.260
Thank you!

06:25.260 --> 06:26.090
Bye-bye!

06:26.090 --> 06:27.540
Be sure to brush your teeth.

06:28.510 --> 06:31.880
You grew up a little by giving 
those kids chocolate, right?

06:31.880 --> 06:33.490
Good for you.

06:33.920 --> 06:34.930
I'm going to buy more.

06:34.930 --> 06:36.090
No, you're not.

06:36.090 --> 06:38.150
We're having a strategy meeting.

06:39.530 --> 06:42.100
Jill said I was free!

06:42.100 --> 06:46.100
Jill? Why bring up that camera nerd now?

06:46.100 --> 06:48.270
She said freedom means 
I can make my own choices.

06:48.270 --> 06:52.110
Hah. Freedom? You know there's no such thing.

06:52.110 --> 06:53.030
There is!

06:53.030 --> 06:54.080
Nope.

06:54.080 --> 06:58.280
Acting on your own free will 
disqualifies you as an agent.

06:58.660 --> 07:01.620
I always fight of my own free will.

07:01.620 --> 07:04.290
All you do is stand behind me and watch!

07:04.290 --> 07:08.760
Don't get smart with the person 
who makes all that possible for you.

07:08.760 --> 07:11.710
You're nothing but a tool for Aletheia.

07:11.710 --> 07:14.000
Just a piece of equipment, really.

07:22.990 --> 07:24.240
Hey...

07:25.930 --> 07:28.030
Welp, she's gone.

07:29.010 --> 07:31.400
Stupid Naomi! Stupid Naomi!

07:31.400 --> 07:34.510
Stupid Naomi! Stupid Naomi! Stupid Naomi!

07:45.920 --> 07:48.040
Stupid, stupid, stupid, stupid.

07:48.040 --> 07:50.040
Stupid, stupid, stupid, stupid.

07:50.040 --> 07:51.600
Stupid, stupid, stupid, stu...

07:51.600 --> 07:52.900
Hey! You just touched me!

07:52.900 --> 07:54.130
I didn't.

07:54.130 --> 07:55.710
You just did! See?

07:55.710 --> 07:59.890
Whew, scary. Imagine a Nean 
touching a human without permission.

07:59.890 --> 08:01.250
It must be broken.

08:01.250 --> 08:03.010
Yeah, definitely broken.

08:03.010 --> 08:05.400
And broken tools must be disposed of.

08:05.400 --> 08:07.600
Please wait a minute. I haven't...

08:07.600 --> 08:09.270
Shut up, Scar Head!

08:09.590 --> 08:11.780
Let's take you to where you'll be dealt with.

08:14.330 --> 08:15.770
Who are you?

08:15.980 --> 08:18.110
What're you lookin' at? Hey!

08:21.570 --> 08:22.490
Bitch!

08:22.920 --> 08:24.160
On the ground! Now!

08:24.550 --> 08:26.330
Neans are not tools.

08:26.330 --> 08:28.080
Or equipment!

08:29.260 --> 08:30.500
What are you?

08:30.500 --> 08:32.000
Rion, what's all this?

08:33.520 --> 08:35.130
Doctor Afdal!

08:35.130 --> 08:37.890
Doctor Afdal. You know this boy?

08:37.890 --> 08:39.640
He's my assistant.

08:39.640 --> 08:41.440
Ah, I see.

08:41.440 --> 08:43.260
That girl over there, too?

08:43.600 --> 08:45.450
Yeah, that's right.

08:46.530 --> 08:49.240
All right, then. Yo, let's go.

08:49.240 --> 08:50.880
What? But...

08:50.880 --> 08:53.650
The doctor's always been good to us.

08:54.030 --> 08:57.290
I'm counting on you to bring us 
the you-know-what again.

08:57.720 --> 08:59.220
C'mon, let's go.

09:00.820 --> 09:03.450
Rion, don't make trouble.

09:03.450 --> 09:05.820
I'm sorry, Doctor.

09:05.820 --> 09:06.830
Let's go.

09:06.830 --> 09:07.710
Yes, sir.

09:11.690 --> 09:12.460
Oh!

09:13.910 --> 09:15.720
Uh, I mean...

09:16.380 --> 09:18.340
O-Over there!

09:19.690 --> 09:21.010
You want in there?

09:22.360 --> 09:24.970
Someone I'm looking for is in there.

09:27.180 --> 09:28.680
Yeah, of course.

09:29.850 --> 09:30.900
Come.

09:31.520 --> 09:32.730
Doctor?

09:34.580 --> 09:35.830
Good work, boys.

09:35.830 --> 09:37.770
Hm? Ah.

09:37.770 --> 09:39.650
Doctor Afdal.

09:55.990 --> 09:57.540
I'm against this.

09:58.020 --> 10:01.220
She may be an Alter. It's too dangerous.

10:01.220 --> 10:03.040
No, she isn't...

10:03.040 --> 10:05.300
Shut up, Nean outsider.

10:05.540 --> 10:08.840
Humans are looking for 
an excuse to destroy us.

10:08.840 --> 10:12.220
There's no need for us to meet 
with an unknown Nean.

10:12.220 --> 10:14.420
No, let's meet with her.

10:14.420 --> 10:15.310
Juval!

10:16.250 --> 10:19.030
What we need is hope.

10:19.030 --> 10:22.570
Even if it's only as much as 
the thinnest spider's thread.

10:35.080 --> 10:36.090
Doctor!

10:36.090 --> 10:37.170
Thank goodness!

10:37.500 --> 10:38.910
Did something happen?

10:38.910 --> 10:41.460
Doctor, we need help! It's Dahlia!

10:44.420 --> 10:45.580
Hold her down!

10:45.580 --> 10:46.220
Yes, sir!

10:46.550 --> 10:47.800
You! Come help!

10:47.800 --> 10:49.270
Quit dawdling!

11:01.660 --> 11:02.580
All good now.

11:02.580 --> 11:03.340
Huh?

11:03.340 --> 11:04.400
Dahlia!

11:06.920 --> 11:10.530
Doctor... Thank you.

11:18.790 --> 11:20.770
Dahlia is stable now.

11:20.770 --> 11:22.610
It's a temporary fix.

11:22.610 --> 11:23.880
She won't get better?

11:24.400 --> 11:27.050
Her signals are out of sync.

11:27.050 --> 11:30.510
But if I let her die, 
her employer will give me hell.

11:30.740 --> 11:32.350
Why would they do that?

11:32.350 --> 11:36.230
People who hire combat 
Neans receive a subsidy.

11:36.740 --> 11:39.650
It means they don't even 
have the freedom to die.

11:40.610 --> 11:42.050
That's cruel.

11:42.050 --> 11:44.110
They're still better off here than elsewhere.

11:44.590 --> 11:47.740
The Neans they're throwing 
at the Venus Project

11:47.740 --> 11:51.040
are being worked to death in 
that planet's harsh environment.

11:51.520 --> 11:56.070
They work only for the 
terraforming of a world

11:56.070 --> 11:59.770
so hellish that humans can't 
touch or even look at it,

11:59.770 --> 12:01.590
and then they die.

12:02.160 --> 12:04.350
They're literally consumable goods.

12:06.920 --> 12:09.970
Anyway, where are you headed?

12:10.560 --> 12:12.880
You said there's someone 
here you're looking for?

12:12.880 --> 12:16.520
Huh? Oh, uh...

12:16.520 --> 12:19.040
Where should I go, I wonder?

12:19.040 --> 12:19.890
Huh?

12:21.430 --> 12:24.860
He's very cunning. I don't know where he is.

12:26.870 --> 12:29.220
You're pretty funny.

12:30.290 --> 12:32.490
You are Rouge, yes?

12:33.050 --> 12:36.870
I am Levi 328 of the CFN.

12:36.870 --> 12:38.500
CF...?

12:38.500 --> 12:40.750
The Council of Free Neans.

12:41.200 --> 12:44.580
I represent someone who 
wishes to meet with you.

12:52.210 --> 12:54.520
What now? At this rate...

12:54.520 --> 12:57.500
Looks like things aren't going your way.

13:03.870 --> 13:05.050
Chief!

13:05.940 --> 13:08.470
About that investigation 
data I asked you for...

13:08.470 --> 13:09.210
Eh?

13:09.210 --> 13:11.360
The case of the red silhouette!

13:11.360 --> 13:13.940
That one that recently showed up 
again in Canal City!

13:13.940 --> 13:16.340
Sorry. I'm busy right now.

13:16.340 --> 13:17.150
Wai—

13:17.150 --> 13:20.110
I'm very sorry. I must ask you to leave.

13:20.610 --> 13:22.980
He's from Ochrona. You sure about this?

13:22.980 --> 13:24.620
Just leave him.

13:24.620 --> 13:25.790
Damn it.

13:26.660 --> 13:29.150
Smoking is prohibited inside this building.

13:29.830 --> 13:31.790
What about those guys, then?

13:33.490 --> 13:34.640
I'll warn them.

13:34.640 --> 13:36.330
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Don't!

13:39.130 --> 13:40.520
I went too far.

13:40.520 --> 13:44.140
A tool for Aletheia? Equipment?

13:44.690 --> 13:47.500
I guess I'm still pretty immature, too.

13:50.450 --> 13:56.070
It seems we'll find a lead on our next target,
Phantom Verde, in the Nean settlement.

13:56.810 --> 13:58.170
Did she go alone?

13:58.930 --> 14:00.320
Nah, no way.

14:00.650 --> 14:03.320
No way... No way?

14:05.780 --> 14:07.240
Huey?

14:07.240 --> 14:08.540
I'm certain of it.

14:09.570 --> 14:12.230
This is the girl I saw 
turning into the red figure.

14:12.790 --> 14:13.970
I see.

14:16.660 --> 14:19.960
Pleasure to meet you, Rouge. I'm Juval.

14:20.430 --> 14:21.440
Uh-huh...

14:22.260 --> 14:25.150
What would the CFN want with a human?

14:25.150 --> 14:26.470
Who knows?

14:26.470 --> 14:29.970
But you keep yourself clear 
of dangerous guys like that.

14:29.970 --> 14:31.600
How can they be dangerous?

14:32.440 --> 14:35.850
We aren't even capable of violence.

14:35.850 --> 14:41.320
The CFN is only trying to win the right 
for Neans to live in freedom.

14:41.320 --> 14:44.260
That's how it starts out, 
no matter who's doing it.

14:44.260 --> 14:47.710
"We only want to live. 
We only want to be free."

14:47.710 --> 14:50.340
Eventually, that's not enough anymore.

14:50.340 --> 14:53.500
Neans are every bit as greedy as humans.

14:53.500 --> 14:55.130
But if nothing else,

14:55.130 --> 14:59.180
humans aren't sent to war 
the moment they're born.

14:59.840 --> 15:04.970
I've only ever known the battlefield, 
this town, and the factory.

15:06.630 --> 15:07.510
Dumas?

15:07.510 --> 15:08.890
Doctor Afdal.

15:09.340 --> 15:10.840
It's been a long time.

15:14.040 --> 15:17.440
After the signing of the ceasefire 
agreement with the Usurpers,

15:17.910 --> 15:22.530
this town was built for the Neans 
returning from the war.

15:23.410 --> 15:27.030
At first, we were permitted 
to govern ourselves.

15:27.710 --> 15:29.450
But now...

15:37.200 --> 15:39.960
The movement for autonomy is at a standstill,

15:40.480 --> 15:43.340
thanks to the wedge driven 
deeply into our consciousness:

15:43.870 --> 15:46.270
the Asimov Code.

15:48.860 --> 15:51.320
We cannot harm humans.

15:51.840 --> 15:54.560
We must obey the orders of humans.

15:55.790 --> 15:57.810
We must protect our own existence.

16:13.940 --> 16:17.450
My third set of parents 
was an old human couple.

16:17.450 --> 16:19.080
They were very kind.

16:20.220 --> 16:24.200
I was made as a substitute child 
for humans who couldn't bear their own.

16:24.680 --> 16:28.570
I have had 23 human parents.

16:29.220 --> 16:33.870
There were some who used Juval, 
a permanent child, for evil.

16:34.270 --> 16:37.110
What did I just say? Some were kind, too.

16:38.270 --> 16:41.810
All we want is to live in freedom.

16:42.590 --> 16:43.820
Freedom...

16:45.900 --> 16:46.820
The Alters...

16:48.520 --> 16:52.280
are a group of Neans who try to 
rebel against humans by force.

16:52.780 --> 16:55.160
There are some like that, yes.

16:55.160 --> 16:57.050
We even have contact with them.

16:57.050 --> 16:59.290
Even with the Asimov Code in place?

16:59.870 --> 17:02.210
I don't really know all the details.

17:02.210 --> 17:05.450
They might be the people I'm chasing after.

17:06.400 --> 17:08.470
You said you can contact them?

17:08.810 --> 17:12.090
They seem to have an informant 
within this settlement.

17:12.760 --> 17:14.720
Do you know who it is?

17:15.850 --> 17:17.020
You do?

17:17.510 --> 17:19.080
Not for certain.

17:19.080 --> 17:20.530
But whoever it is...

17:21.560 --> 17:26.270
What we seek is not your strength.

17:26.270 --> 17:28.110
It's your free will.

17:29.670 --> 17:31.670
You aren't bound by the Asimov Code.

17:31.670 --> 17:34.140
You interact with humans as an equal.

17:34.140 --> 17:37.020
That gives your existence 
itself great meaning.

17:37.930 --> 17:43.690
Even just knowing that a Nean like you 
exists and walks in step with us

17:43.690 --> 17:46.420
will give many Neans hope.

17:47.280 --> 17:49.840
Give Neans... hope?

17:50.310 --> 17:53.460
Of course, you don't need 
to answer right away.

17:53.800 --> 17:57.730
Take your time thinking about it 
during your stay here.

18:01.670 --> 18:05.940
Well, then, Doctor Afdal, 
I'll be counting on you.

18:08.770 --> 18:11.170
He's as full of shit as ever.

18:13.280 --> 18:14.410
Doctor!

18:14.690 --> 18:16.810
It's... It's Dahlia!

18:22.020 --> 18:24.380
I'm sure she's grateful to you.

18:24.970 --> 18:27.950
The battlefield, this town, and the factory...

18:27.950 --> 18:30.600
She said those were all she ever knew.

18:31.510 --> 18:33.830
This city is all I know.

18:34.760 --> 18:39.670
I've lived here, helping you, 
ever since I was born.

18:40.660 --> 18:44.370
If I can learn techniques from you 
that I can use to help my kind...

18:44.790 --> 18:48.750
What did I tell you? 
That's always how it starts.

18:48.750 --> 18:50.040
But soon...

18:50.700 --> 18:52.570
that won't be enough.

18:56.280 --> 18:57.720
Doctor?

18:59.010 --> 19:00.160
Tools.

19:00.710 --> 19:01.790
Equipment.

19:02.340 --> 19:03.460
Freedom.

19:04.050 --> 19:05.530
Hope...

19:09.640 --> 19:13.020
I wonder what Naomi would say.

19:13.720 --> 19:14.740
Excuse me.

19:16.920 --> 19:18.600
Juval wishes to see you.

19:23.130 --> 19:24.270
Bingo!

19:24.500 --> 19:27.030
She got into the settlement on her own!

19:27.030 --> 19:28.840
She's more competent than I thought!

19:33.780 --> 19:36.360
He said to have you come in alone.

19:36.360 --> 19:37.460
Thanks.

19:57.540 --> 19:59.350
<i>What the heck are you doing?</i>

20:00.920 --> 20:02.720
I didn't do it!

20:02.720 --> 20:05.840
<i>I know that. So who's the kid?</i>

20:06.320 --> 20:07.440
Juval.

20:07.700 --> 20:08.600
Juval?

20:08.600 --> 20:10.420
Juval...

20:10.420 --> 20:11.970
Juval 087...

20:11.970 --> 20:14.400
Dang, he's a big fish!

20:14.680 --> 20:15.720
Juval!

20:17.930 --> 20:19.660
Don't tell me you...

20:19.660 --> 20:21.240
Everyone, calm down.

20:24.490 --> 20:26.970
Let's keep this quiet for a while.

20:26.970 --> 20:27.790
But...!

20:27.790 --> 20:32.290
If the humans find out, 
they'll try to meddle in our affairs.

20:33.340 --> 20:34.510
Well...

20:36.660 --> 20:39.300
Hm? Ah, Doctor. Is something the matter?

20:43.920 --> 20:45.060
Chief!

20:45.060 --> 20:46.700
What's all the fuss?

20:46.700 --> 20:49.040
I'm sending a security force 
to the Nean settlement.

20:49.040 --> 20:49.940
What happened?

20:49.940 --> 20:53.270
Ochrona or not, this area 
is under our jurisdiction.

20:53.550 --> 20:55.680
I'd prefer it if you stayed out of this.

20:56.210 --> 20:58.420
Aren't we both public servants?

20:58.420 --> 20:59.800
Excuse me.

21:02.430 --> 21:05.160
Did she get set up by those Alter guys?

21:06.260 --> 21:08.080
What should I do?
